WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.800
In News of the World, a Civil War veteran&nbsp;
played by Tom Hanks decides to take a young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.320
orphan girl across Texas in 1870 so she can be&nbsp;
reunited with family members she's never known.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.720
This is the end of News of the World explained.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.480
When we meet Captain Jefferson&nbsp;
Kyle Kidd, he feels like a man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.480
a bit untethered from the world around him.
Over the course of News of the World, Kidd's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.960
relationship with Johanna helps to transform him&nbsp;
into a man with something to care about again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.840
He sees Johanna as not just a challenge he's eager&nbsp;
to surmount, but an eager and curious spirit who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.840
complements his own desire to share his knowledge&nbsp;
with the rest of the world. We don't know what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.160
awaits them in the future, but it's clear from&nbsp;
the film's final scene that Kidd is a changed man.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.400
When we meet Kidd, he's making his&nbsp;
living as a professional reader of news,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.880
but his job is about more than merely reading&nbsp;
from a newspaper. He's a curator, an orator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.640
and a showman, and his interest in the kinds&nbsp;
of stories he wants to tell shifts along with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.640
the film, as he delivers everything&nbsp;
from delightful romps to hard news.
 &nbsp;

00:00:54.640 --> 00:01:00.000
"Ladies and gentlemen, my name is Captain&nbsp;
Jefferson Kyle Kidd and I'm here tonight to read&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.320
the news from across this great world of ours."
 
So what does that mean for Kidd's professional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.240
future? By the end of the film he's happily&nbsp;
news-reading with Johanna by his side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.360
but he also mentions his past as&nbsp;
the owner of a printing company,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.360
something it seems like he'd be very good at with&nbsp;
the right financial backing. We know from history&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.920
that men who get paid to deliver the news don't&nbsp;
go away. They just evolve with the technology.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.080
So will Kidd evolve his news-reading to change&nbsp;
with the times? Will he go back to printing?

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.360
The young girl known as Cicada to her Kiowa&nbsp;
family and Johanna to her German family is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:32.800
an intriguing puzzle throughout News of&nbsp;
the World. And yet we do get to see an arc&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.280
unfolding through her nonverbal communication as&nbsp;
Johanna shifts from being desperately sad to lose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.200
her Kiowa family to confused and angered&nbsp;
by her German family to eager and happy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.880
to be with Kidd for the rest of her life.
Still, the question remains what exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.760
Johanna's future truly holds. Given that&nbsp;
she's essentially the child of two worlds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.080
it would not be hard to see her as an advocate for&nbsp;
Native American rights as an adult, fighting for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.080
social justice with her adoptive father's passion&nbsp;
for knowledge supporting her along the way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.400
Even if that's not the path she takes, though,&nbsp;
she has a bright and loving future ahead.
 &nbsp;

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.320
"See all those words? Put&nbsp;
them all together and you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.280
have a story."

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:14.400
News of the World is set in 1870, five years after&nbsp;
the end of the American Civil War, in a state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.200
that's found it particularly difficult to keep&nbsp;
up with the reconstruction era. Violent racism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.840
remains rampant, roads everywhere are dangerous,&nbsp;
and people are willing to do just about anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.640
to survive or to profit off others. Very early on&nbsp;
in the film, Kidd tells us that he is a part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:33.040
this aftermath in a no small way, having been&nbsp;
a soldier in Texas who didn't surrender until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:37.680
weeks after the death of Abraham Lincoln. He is&nbsp;
a product of this time, and he suffers for it.&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:41.120
But of course, we know the history of&nbsp;
Reconstruction. What the film is more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:46.080
interested in showing us is an intimate look at&nbsp;
the human cost, because as Kidd later explains, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.400
was off fighting a war on behalf of other people,&nbsp;
and all he got for his trouble were some scars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:54.480
and the fact that he wasn't there for the death&nbsp;
of his wife. There was a tremendous economic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:59.280
political, and social cost to the American&nbsp;
Civil War, some of which we still feel today.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.080
But it also left a more human carnage behind,&nbsp;
psychological scarring that wasn't easily healed.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:10.000
News of the World is, at its core, a story of&nbsp;
two people who have both lost their family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.200
Johanna is, as Kidd eventually&nbsp;
learns, an orphan two times over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.320
having lost her birth parents when she&nbsp;
was too young to really remember them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.840
and then losing her adoptive parents at the&nbsp;
hands of people who thought they were saving her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.560
Kidd, for his part, is also without a family,&nbsp;
traveling around and making plenty of friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:29.040
across Texas even as he refuses to go&nbsp;
home to reckon with the loss of his wife.&nbsp;

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.280
Both of them are on a journey of reconciliation,&nbsp;
one that truly picks up steam when Johanna makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:38.480
a choice. Faced with the prospect of rejoining&nbsp;
a group of Kiowa who just happen to be traveling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:43.360
nearby, she instead asks them for a horse, brings&nbsp;
it back to Kidd, and keeps traveling with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.720
It takes a little longer for Kidd to&nbsp;
catch up to her emotional wavelength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.600
but the message is clear. This is the moment when&nbsp;
she decides that he is her family, and because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:56.240
he ultimately makes the same choice, they can&nbsp;
both find their taste for familial love again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:00.480
The entire movie hinges on that choice, when&nbsp;
she asks to stay rather than to go, and it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:06.240
perfectly sets up the final moments of the film.
